  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `createdAt` and `amountCents` to `OrderPlaced` and kept the old ones. All 39 tests pass and the type check is clean.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event, so renames have to go through deprecation. Removing `placedAt` and `totalCents` outright could break them.\n\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now carries `createdAt` (same value as `placedAt`) and `amountCents` (same value as `totalCents`). `placedAt` and `totalCents` are marked `@deprecated` and still sent. `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` now check both the new and the old fields.\n- **HTTP responses:** I left them alone. `GET /orders/{id}` still returns `placedAt` and `totalCents` (ARCH-8), and the rename was only asked for on the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consumer teams need to move to the new names. After that, a follow-up change can drop `placedAt` and `totalCents`, and you'll probably want to bump `schemaVersion` then. If billing-service and analytics-ingest have already migrated, tell me and I can do the removal now.",
